  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LGBT+ Access to Justice in Serbia: Acknowledging victims, ensuring prosecution, and making incidents visible.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project tackles the issue of access to justice for LGBT+ people in Serbia that builds up on organization&#x2019;s previously established (and recently improved) monitoring system for mapping and documenting unlawful conducts against queer folks, that has been running for five consecutive years. The aim is to deepen the cooperation with relevant state stakeholders - to convey training and best practices to the relevant competent authorities and law enforcement agencies, and to create a Protocol for Prosecutors on how to deal with the cases of unlawful conducts due to SOGI.The project will continue to provide legal support, in accordance with the Law on Free Legal Support of the Republic of Serbia, with the aim of establishing case law (which, after almost a decade, is still virtually non-existent) and conducting relevant legal disputes. Further to this, the implementing organization will continue to monitor and document cases, publish Annual Report on Hate-motivated Unlawful Conduct against LGBT+ persons and will conduct a nationwide social media campaign to promote their work, with a special focus on queer people living in smaller places and cities.</narrative>
  </description>
